			},
			"date": "2026-05-17T14:48:48.417Z",
			"content": "<p>Is it renting? Or is it more like a condo?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4hm2yozxzsakerfalloor5s6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mm2myg3bss24",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mm2lxbzbvs2o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/anatudor.bsky.social/post/3mm2myg3bss24",
			"author": {
				"name": "Ana Tudor",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/anatudor.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4hm2yozxzsakerfalloor5s6/bafkreicqw7fxgwhrsestevru7zj4yazlcdfhibmuc2kvnllcf4mwbykeca"
			},
			"date": "2026-05-17T15:02:40.349Z",
			"content": "<p>That's completely irrelevant. The only thing it matters is that it costs money. Regularly. And recurrent expenses are to be avoided at all costs when you don't have much of a recurrent income.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:kn5hbzh6ig6qla64l5puqapb/app.bsky.feed.post/3mm2myxl2vk2d",
			"parentId": 0,
